    <item>
      <title>Orbit 2026.11.8.0615</title>
      <pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 06:15:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>202611080615</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2026.11.8.0615</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <sparkle:releaseNotesLink>https://github.com/siosphere/orbit-updates/releases/tag/v202611080615</sparkle:releaseNotesLink>
      <orbit:note>Ctrl+T, New Tab, and Ctrl+L now open a command bar on Windows.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>The old welcome heading and buttons now fully disappear before the profile cards slide in.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>Windows now has the address pill and Find in Page (Ctrl+F).</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>Your sign-in tokens and sync key are now stored in Windows Credential Manager instead of plain files.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>Opening a link while Orbit is running now adds a tab instead of starting a second instance.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>You can now set Orbit as your default browser from the menu, and uninstalling removes that setting.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>Downloads from the web now save to your Downloads folder, with a panel to track and cancel them.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>Windows now has a Settings window where you can turn sync on, join, or off.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>File ▸ Import from Browser… and Import from Arc… now show a step-by-step card instead of a picker with checkboxes.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>Chromium's flags page (View ▸ Developer ▸ Chromium Flags, or chrome://flags) now opens in Orbit, and its Relaunch button restarts Orbit to apply them.</orbit:note>
      <orbit:note>…and 1 more change</orbit:note>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/siosphere/orbit-updates/releases/download/v202611080615/Orbit-202611080615.zip" length="160243243" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="iSvHsMC7jWlS2xjgt+iyC+oB7LwChPcd3ArzxT5MxlNoO50c6yPrnRu233g3GnCKbZZSmMyZxtMEETXAQPNCDA=="></enclosure>
